# imp-rust coverage

When you modify imp-rust implementation or tests under `.mnt/imp-rust/`:

1. Run **`bash scripts/coverage-imp-rust.sh --changed`** from the silentorb-workbench root (one batched container: test + llvm-cov).
2. Include the printed **coverage summary** in your final response.
3. If changed files or their crate are below **`line_target`** in `.mnt/imp-rust/coverage-targets.toml`, add or extend **integration tests** under `crates/<crate>/tests/` before finishing (unless the user explicitly waives tests).
4. Prefer **`coverage-imp-rust.sh`** over separate `run-in-imp-rust.sh test` and `run-in-imp-rust.sh llvm-cov` calls (avoids extra ephemeral container spin-ups).
5. Tests use the crate **public API** only — see `.mnt/imp-rust/docs/rust-style.md`.

Commands:

- `bash scripts/run-in-imp-rust.sh test` — cargo only (ephemeral container when workbench has no local rust)
- `bash scripts/coverage-imp-rust.sh --changed` — batched test + coverage + report (preferred after edits)

Targets and baseline: `.mnt/imp-rust/docs/coverage.md`
